In-Reply-To: <822VuZpIgAU.UC_7p4MhEwAJ@ctmm-user.groups.google.com>
References: <822VuZpIgAU.UC_7p4MhEwAJ@ctmm-user.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ctmm-user/c/822VuZpIgAU/m/bwcXdlGEEQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Stephanie,

ctmm.fit() returns a model of the same class as the guess argument. By default from ctmm.guess(), this is an OUF model with anisotropic covariance.

There are some other examples in the MEE Application paper: https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/2041-210X.12559

Best,
Chris

